<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - April 7.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - April 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	350.69   7.61</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	  252.08   1.21</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	  237.36   2.16</p>
<p> 4   Ranger Minerals     200.96   4.20</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	 197.67   0.85</p>
<p> 6   Equatorial Min	138.89   0.25</p>
<p> 7   Westpac Prop Tr     107.50   1.72</p>
<p> 8   St.Barbara Mine     107.04   0.76</p>
<p> 9   Consol Paper	   86.47   2.94</p>
<p>10   Devex		    75.56   0.34</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	   1.75   0.87</p>
<p> 2   Jardine Fm China	4.37   0.65</p>
<p> 3   Consol Rutile	   4.59   1.03</p>
<p> 4   Premier Inv	     5.52   1.30</p>
<p> 5   BTR Plc		   5.53   5.15</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.85   0.98</p>
<p> 7   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	 7.13   0.72</p>
<p> 8   Renison Goldflds	7.16   4.88</p>
<p> 9   Adel Bton Cement	7.30   1.75</p>
<p>10   FAI Life Ltd	    7.45   0.74</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
